  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1028 PM CST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nDespite the active pattern across the CONUS this week, relatively\nbenign conditions are expected across our area. The upper low \nwill finally depart on Tuesday, with light WSW winds helping to \nbring highs a degree or two warmer from Monday. An upper trough \nand associated surface cold front will move through on Wednesday \nwith surface winds switching out of the north. However given the \ntime of year, the airmass will not bring the much cooler \ntemperatures we would see as we approach meteorological winter and\nhighs will be similar as Tuesday. Additional increased mid-level \nnortherly flow between the aforementioned trough and a building \nridge to the west will drop highs a couple degrees thereafter \ninto the next weekend. Precipitation chances may return later in \nthe weekend into early next week with an upper low approaching\nfrom the west.",
